{"session_id":"svc-1778625576170598762","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-12T22:39:46.311182935Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","sticky":{"key_present":true,"bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"requested_harness":"codex","resolved_harness":"codex","harness_source":"request_harness","requested_model":"gpt-5.4-mini","resolved_model":"gpt-5.4-mini","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-b76d6a2c-20260512T223933-2fe233a3","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead inside an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the completion contract — every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file you can point to after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs as separate deliverables.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized sub-pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, treat Step 0 as a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, decomposed children once more; third-level splits must be rejected with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose — do not attempt the work:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child slice (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a success. Do not mix implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;`.ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3/no_changes_rationale.txt` must contain one:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` reject.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;To request orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and project defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-b76d6a2c\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003ebench: clean shutdown — kill -TERM sweep reaps the whole process tree\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nKilling a sweep parent (run_terminalbench_2_1_sweep.sh PID) does not currently kill its descendant matrix-runner / harbor children. They are reparented to init (PPID=1) and keep executing. Concrete failures this session:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. **2026-05-11 ~22:30Z** — Killed the local-lane sweep (PID 463900). Vidar matrix-runner child kept running on the dead oMLX server, wasted 70 cells with retry-spam pattern before I noticed.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;2. **2026-05-11 ~18:15Z** — Killed the timing-baseline ds4 sweep (PID 942197) after the reasoning-not-supported bug. The matrix-runner became orphan (945491, PPID=1). Then I launched a replacement (991522 → 999500) and a second iteration (975660, orphan). All three were running simultaneously against ds4\u0026#39;s single graph worker, contending for the slot and writing to the same report.json paths. Smoke tests timed out because of slot contention. Took ~30 min to notice and clean up.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The general pattern: any time we `kill -KILL \u0026lt;sweep_pid\u0026gt;` to restart with new config (multiplier change, profile fix, server-side issue), one or more children survive. They consume identical work, race the new sweep, and corrupt the per-cell results.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Two interlocking pieces:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A. **run_terminalbench_2_1_sweep.sh: trap signals + propagate.** Add a trap handler in the shell script that on SIGTERM/SIGINT/EXIT:\u0026#xA;   - Records the matrix-runner PIDs as they spawn\u0026#xA;   - On signal, sends SIGTERM to each matrix-runner PID; if still alive after 10s, SIGKILL\u0026#xA;   - Then exits\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;B. **cmd/bench (sweep + matrix subcommands): handle SIGTERM by killing harbor children.** When fiz-bench receives SIGTERM, propagate to in-flight `harbor run` subprocesses (exec.CommandContext already supports this via context cancellation). The existing `cmd.Cancel = func() error { return cmd.Process.Signal(syscall.SIGTERM) }` is correct shape; verify it actually fires on parent SIGTERM and not just on context.WithTimeout.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;C. **Alternative (single-knob fix): process groups.** Have the sweep script start fiz-bench in its own process group (`setpgid`), and have the kill path send SIGTERM to the entire process group (`kill -TERM -\u0026lt;pgid\u0026gt;`). One signal takes out the whole tree atomically. Simpler than A+B; downside is no graceful per-process shutdown order.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files:\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/run_terminalbench_2_1_sweep.sh — trap handler + PID tracking\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/sweep.go and cmd/bench/matrix.go — signal handling on the Go side (verify existing exec.CommandContext + cmd.Cancel work as intended on SIGTERM, not just context cancel)\u0026#xA;- Tests / integration: confirm a `kill -TERM $sweep_pid` reaps the entire process tree within 30s.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope:\u0026#xA;- Persistent state recovery (sweep resume from interrupted cell). Already handled by --resume + report.json being the durable state.\u0026#xA;- Distinguishing \u0026#34;user-initiated kill\u0026#34; from \u0026#34;supervisor-initiated kill\u0026#34; — both should cleanly shut down.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ACCEPTANCE IS A COMMAND\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `bash scripts/benchmark/run_terminalbench_2_1_sweep.sh --phase canary --lanes ds4 \u0026amp;` then `kill $!` results in ZERO surviving fiz-bench or harbor processes within 30s (verify via `pgrep -f \u0026#34;fiz-bench|harbor run\u0026#34;`).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;2. Same scenario but `kill -TERM` — the shutdown is graceful: each in-flight cell\u0026#39;s harbor invocation gets SIGTERM (lets it tear down its docker-compose stack via the existing `--delete` finalizer, see cmd/bench/matrix.go cmd.Cancel handler), waits up to 60s for it to finish, then exits.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;3. New integration test scripts/benchmark/test_sweep_shutdown.bash spawns a sweep, sends SIGTERM, asserts (a) all sweep-related processes are gone within 60s, (b) report.json files for in-flight cells are either complete or absent (no half-written state).\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. `TestSweepShutdownKillReapsProcessTree` covers `bash scripts/benchmark/run_terminalbench_2_1_sweep.sh --phase canary --lanes ds4 \u0026amp;` followed by `kill $!`, leaving zero surviving `fiz-bench` or `harbor run` processes within 30s as verified with `pgrep -f \u0026#34;fiz-bench|harbor run\u0026#34;`.\u0026#xA;2. `TestSweepShutdownTermGraceful` covers `kill -TERM $!`, proving each in-flight Harbor invocation receives SIGTERM, can run docker-compose teardown through the existing `--delete` finalizer, waits up to 60s, then exits.\u0026#xA;3. `TestSweepShutdownNoOrphans` in `scripts/benchmark/test_sweep_shutdown.bash` spawns a sweep, sends SIGTERM, and asserts all sweep-related processes are gone within 60s.\u0026#xA;4. `TestSweepShutdownReportState` in `scripts/benchmark/test_sweep_shutdown.bash` asserts report.json files for in-flight cells are either complete or absent, with no half-written state.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003cnotes\u003e\nOperator made ACs mechanically verifiable with explicit test names and cleared stale AC-quality gate metadata.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Review 2026-05-12: bash scripts/benchmark/test_sweep_shutdown.bash fails locally, timing out waiting for fake-harbor started; process-tree shutdown is not end-to-end verified.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Review 2026-05-12 final pass: timeout 120s bash scripts/benchmark/test_sweep_shutdown.bash failed locally at TestSweepShutdownKillReapsProcessTree: timed out waiting for log fake-harbor started. Parent fizeau-1a5353cd remains open until the named shell acceptance test passes reliably.\n    \u003c/notes\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:benchmark, kind:reliability, kind:tooling, triage:no-changes-unjustified\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-1a5353cd\" base-rev=\"7f93c955e19f9519416850d2a741077b92e47157\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read those before editing. Ground decisions in what is already in the repository; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","attempt_id":"20260512T223933-2fe233a3","base_rev":"7f93c955e19f9519416850d2a741077b92e47157","bead_id":"fizeau-b76d6a2c","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3","correlation_id":"fizeau-b76d6a2c:20260512T223933-2fe233a3","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260512T223933-2fe233a3/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"96c13f1a0f1fcb04454445c32e42e3bfede3d8c9526f406688f44a62777d51f3","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-9c272b87","worker_id":""}}}
